{
  "id": "28924_kagameru",
  "headword": "{屈|かが}める",
  "reading": "かがめる",
  "romaji": "kagameru",
  "part_of_speech": "verb (ichidan)",
  "gloss": "to bend (one's back, body); to stoop",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to bend (one's back or body); to stoop down",
      "explanation": "To bend a part of one's own body — usually the back, knees, or whole body — to lower oneself or duck under something. The object is one's own body part."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "28924_kagameru_ex1",
      "japanese": "{身|み}を{屈|かが}めた。",
      "english": "I bent down.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "28924_kagameru_ex2",
      "japanese": "{低|ひく}い{戸口|とぐち}で{頭|あたま}を{屈|かが}めて{入|はい}った。",
      "english": "I ducked my head to enter through the low doorway.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "28924_kagameru_ex3",
      "japanese": "{祖父|そふ}は{腰|こし}を{屈|かが}めて{庭|にわ}の{雑草|ざっそう}を{抜|ぬ}いている。",
      "english": "My grandfather is stooping over and pulling weeds in the garden.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Transitive counterpart of {屈|かが}む (to crouch, to stoop). Where {屈|かが}む describes the body crouching as a whole, {屈|かが}める takes a specific body part as object.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\nTransitive (takes を). The object is always one's own body part — {身|み}, {腰|こし}, {頭|あたま}, {膝|ひざ}.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {身|み}を{屈|かが}める: to bend one's body; to crouch down\n- {腰|こし}を{屈|かが}める: to bend at the waist; to stoop\n- {頭|あたま}を{屈|かが}める: to duck one's head\n- {膝|ひざ}を{屈|かが}める: to bend one's knees\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {屈|かが}む: to crouch; to stoop — intransitive pair\n- {曲|ま}げる: to bend (something) — general, can take any object\n- しゃがむ: to squat down — fully lower to a squatting position",
  "schema_version": "2.0",
